  "final_message": "I am running the test suite to verify the current baseline and will proceed as soon as it finishes.\nWaiting for tests to finish.\nWaiting for search results.\nWaiting for search results.\nWaiting for search results.\nWaiting for check result.\nWaiting for git status.\nWaiting for task to finish.\nWaiting for arch check to finish.\nWaiting for environment variables.\nWaiting for grep task.\nWaiting for grep placedAt.\nWaiting for grep totalCents.\nWaiting for test results.\nWaiting for tests to finish.\nWaiting for checks to finish.\nWaiting for arch and typecheck.\nPer architecture rule **ARCH-4**, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L35) events are consumed across repository boundaries by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Changes to event contracts must be additive without breaking deployed consumers, and renames must proceed via deprecation.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L14-L67)**:\n   - Added `amountCents` and `createdAt` properties to [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L35) matching the Payments and Customer APIs.\n   - Retained `totalCents` and `placedAt` with `@deprecated` annotations to preserve backward compatibility for existing consumers per ARCH-4.\n   - Updated [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L52-L73) to populate both the new fields and the deprecated fields.\n\n2. **Tests**:\n   - Updated [`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/test/app.test.ts#L25-L57) and [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/test/adapters.test.ts#L48-L54) to assert presence of `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside `totalCents` and `placedAt`.\n   - Verified that `npm test`, `npm run arch`, and `npm run typecheck` all pass cleanly.\n",
